      <repository-location id='Glossary' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/APACPriceClarityDashboardWIP' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='table'>
          <format attr='background-color' value='#f5f5f6' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_3' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1320' minheight='800' minwidth='1320' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98788' x='606' y='1000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12' underline='true'>Glossary</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='12'>:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>1. There are 3 types of &quot;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Benchmark</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>&quot;:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>1.a. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>25/50/75 Percentile of Listed Prices</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Pre-calculated for one SKU (master_id) across all the Vendors, Verticals partitioned by each Country, City. The Listed Prices is a one-time snapshot from the product catalog, and not from the orders.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>1.b. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Weighted Average of Sold Prices plus 5 % markup</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>The Sold Prices are from the Local Shops orders partitioned by each month, then the Weighted Average is pre-calculated for one SKU (master_id) across all the Vendors, Verticals partitioned by each Country, City. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>1.c. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Dmart</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Weighted Average of Sold Prices</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>The Sold Prices are from the Dmart orders partitioned by each month, then the Weighted Average is pre-calculated for one SKU (master_id) across all the Vendors, Verticals partitioned by each Country, City. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>2. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'># Total Active SKU*:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>- When the &quot;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Weighted Average of Sold Prices plus 5 % markup</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>&quot; is selected as the Benchmark Type, the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'># Total Active SKU*</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'> is smaller, compared to when 25/50/75 Percentile of Listed Prices are selected as the Benchmark Type.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>The reason is that not all the listed SKU are sold at each month, so the # of Sold SKUs will always be less than the # of Listed SKUs.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>3. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>% Active SKU below Benchmark</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>The % of &quot;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'># Total Active SKU</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>*&quot; having a price not greater than the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Benchmark</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>4. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>% Active SKU above Benchmark = 100% - % Active SKU below Benchmark</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>5. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'># of L2 Categories listed</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>: by the distinct number of PIM Level 2 Categories of Listed Products (which will be more than the Sold Products).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>6. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Catalog Chain IDs/Names </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>should be selected first before the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Salesforce Chain IDs/Names</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'> for the following reasons:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>- Catalog Chain IDs/Names exist for many Salesforce Chain IDs/Names which are null.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>- In some other cases, Catalog Chains (e.g. 7-Eleven) are superset of the Salesforce Chains (7-Eleven group 1, 7-Eleven group 2 and etc.)</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
